1
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:32,450
Mr. Lee, if you had taken a taxi all the way home,
you probably wouldn't have made it to work tomorrow.

2
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:39,290
We worked late into the night,
and I'm sorry to intrude on your home, Mr. Kang.

3
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:43,790
Intrude? It's better than being alone.

4
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:47,590
Sleep on the couch in the living room. I'll get you a blanket.

5
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:25,039
Why are you looking at me like that?
I said go wash up.

6
00:01:29,210 --> 00:01:31,260
Mr. Kang...

7
00:01:32,470 --> 00:01:33,930
What?

8
00:01:36,759 --> 00:01:39,020
Can I really...

9
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:42,890
just sleep on the couch?

10
00:01:55,660 --> 00:02:00,200
Ko Taewoon / Kim Dohyun

11
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:16,760
Baek Seunghoon / Lee Kyungwon

12
00:02:28,270 --> 00:02:35,700
Twisted Tie

13
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:38,990
Episode 1. The Team Leader's Office Perks

14
00:03:10,110 --> 00:03:13,990
- Mr. Lee.
- Yes, Mr. Kang.

15
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:20,490
You call this a proposal for the VVIP Ocean View Lounge?

16
00:03:20,490 --> 00:03:23,329
Is this traffic flow the best you can do?

17
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:32,750
Does the client have to walk down this narrow hallway
staring only at imported marble walls?

18
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:40,760
Is a pretty design everything?

19
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:44,350
You have absolutely no understanding of the space right now.

20
00:03:45,770 --> 00:03:47,520
I apologize.

21
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:52,690
I was so focused on the point wall
that I missed checking the traffic flow.

22
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:01,780
Spend your time coming up with a revision instead of making excuses.

23
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:05,370
Yes, I will redo it right away.

24
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:15,340
Mr. Kang, he's a rookie.
Aren't you being a bit too hard on him?

25
00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:18,839
Mr. Lee was tearing up a bit earlier.

26
00:04:18,839 --> 00:04:23,970
Do clients pay less because he's a rookie?

27
00:04:26,810 --> 00:04:32,360
If you baby him, he'll stay at that level forever.

28
00:04:35,110 --> 00:04:38,320
[Weather Agency - Heavy Rain & Thunderstorm Warning]
Heavy localized rain and thunderstorms across Seoul around 9 PM tonight.

29
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:10,310
Mr. Lee, don't take it to heart.

30
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:15,520
The whole team knows Mr. Kang is a cold-blooded perfectionist
who wouldn't bleed a drop if you pricked him.

31
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:21,740
- Exactly, you're just a rookie.
- Honestly, doesn't Mr. Kang seem to have a bit of a sociopath in him?

32
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:28,580
Just because he's perfect, does he think everyone is a robot?
You must have felt so unfairly treated, Mr. Lee.

33
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,750
No.

34
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:33,540
Actually, everyone.

35
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:37,420
I have to disagree with what you just said.

36
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:42,680
- I was just trying to take your side...
- Mr. Kang was exactly right.

37
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:48,560
I got so obsessed with the point wall that
I completely ruined the basic client traffic flow.

38
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:52,480
Just because a design is pretty
doesn't make it a good space.

39
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:55,480
I made a very amateur mistake.

40
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:59,610
He might not be wrong, but his words are a bit cold...

41
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:03,740
He's not cold, he's rational.

42
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:07,580
When he said that babying someone keeps them at that level,

43
00:06:08,490 --> 00:06:13,500
it genuinely hit me like a ton of bricks.
I had a huge realization.

44
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:18,670
I don't know how he pinpoints the core issue
without a single margin of error...

45
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:20,800
He is truly amazing.

46
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:27,220
- Are you being gaslit by Mr. Kang?
- It's a severe case. That's quite a talent.

47
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:31,270
That's right, I need to work my fingers to the bone
to meet Mr. Kang's standards.

48
00:06:31,270 --> 00:06:36,270
I'm going to completely redo the 3D rendering right now.
Keep up the good work.

49
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:42,860
What's up with him?

50
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:48,450
I think a crazy guy just joined our team.

51
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:11,760
Great work today, everyone.

52
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:14,640
Those who went out for afternoon meetings can leave right away,

53
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:18,940
and the rest of you, just finish up what you're doing
and head home early.

54
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:22,900
- Yes, great work.
- I'll be leaving first.

55
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:25,320
Great work today.

56
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,320
What are you doing after this?

57
00:07:30,370 --> 00:07:33,370
- Mr. Lee.
- Yes?

58
00:07:34,750 --> 00:07:38,750
Mr. Lee, make sure you get this approved today
before you leave.

59
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:44,260
In order for Mr. Baek to order the imported materials,
it needs to be finalized by tomorrow morning.

60
00:07:44,260 --> 00:07:47,760
Ah... um, by today?

61
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:55,600
Ah, to run the 3D rendering again,
it'll probably take past midnight...

62
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,890
Why?

63
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:00,560
Do you have a problem with that?

64
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:05,030
Ah, no.
I will definitely finish it by today.

65
00:08:05,030 --> 00:08:07,070
Please go ahead and leave first.

66
00:08:07,860 --> 00:08:13,030
I'll be staying too.
I need to approve it as soon as it's done.

67
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:07,960
Mr. Kang.

68
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:15,600
The rendering for the revision is complete.
Could you take a look?

69
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:23,810
It's already midnight.
Good job, Sunwoo. Let's see.

70
00:09:40,710 --> 00:09:44,830
Wow... It's pouring down hard.

71
00:09:46,090 --> 00:09:50,630
Mr. Lee, where did you say you lived?

72
00:09:53,550 --> 00:09:57,010
- Was it around Gimpo?
- Ah, yes.

73
00:09:57,010 --> 00:10:00,890
Ah, but with this much rain at this hour,

74
00:10:00,890 --> 00:10:04,100
I'm not sure if I can catch a taxi.

75
00:10:07,110 --> 00:10:09,400
Even if you catch one, it's a problem.

76
00:10:10,030 --> 00:10:14,740
The Olympic Expressway is probably completely flooded by now.

77
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:20,870
Ah, I should look for a nearby sauna.
I have a morning meeting tomorrow, and if I'm late...

78
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:25,540
If you go to a sauna, how are you going to come to work
smelling like sweat tomorrow?

79
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:40,510
I refuse to see my team member face a client
in a wrinkled shirt, reeking of sweat.

80
00:10:46,850 --> 00:10:50,020
Pack your bag.
We're going to my place.

81
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:54,240
Ah... Ah, no.
How could I go to your place, Mr. Kang... I'll figure it out...

82
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:59,370
Mr. Lee.
I hate repeating myself.

83
00:11:00,330 --> 00:11:05,830
My place is 5 minutes from here,
so just follow me without another word.

84
00:11:43,450 --> 00:11:47,370
Why are you looking at me like that? I said go wash up.

85
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:53,840
What?

86
00:11:56,420 --> 00:12:01,600
Can I really just sleep on the couch?

87
00:12:17,950 --> 00:12:23,620
- You're crossing the line, Mr. Lee.
- Mr. Kang.

88
00:12:28,250 --> 00:12:34,170
Stop talking nonsense and just go in and wash up.
You'll catch a cold.

89
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:38,720
Ah, I'm- I'm sorry.
Ah, I must have been crazy for a second.

90
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:42,300
The towels are in the cabinet.

91
00:12:44,050 --> 00:12:46,770
Yes, thank you.

92
00:13:29,230 --> 00:13:31,770
Mr. Kang's scent...

93
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:41,700
Ah, I must be crazy. Seriously, what's wrong with me?

94
00:14:00,970 --> 00:14:06,100
Lee Sunwoo, this is Mr. Kang Dojin's house.

95
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:08,760
He's your team leader.

96
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:18,190
Just quietly breathe and sleep.

97
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:25,030
Just sleep on the couch, quietly breathing.
Yeah, I can do this.

98
00:14:54,390 --> 00:14:58,610
The clothes look really tight on you.
That must be uncomfortable.

99
00:14:58,610 --> 00:15:03,030
Ah, no.
The... scent is nice too,

100
00:15:03,030 --> 00:15:05,610
and it's extremely comfortable... Yes.

101
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:15,210
Don't just stand there, come and sit down.

102
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:37,140
Mr. Kang,

103
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:42,570
you give off a very different vibe
like this.

104
00:15:46,490 --> 00:15:50,160
If I acted like Team Leader Kang Dojin outside of work,

105
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:53,240
how could anyone live without suffocating?

106
00:15:58,580 --> 00:16:01,460
You worked hard today, Sunwoo.

107
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,250
What?

108
00:16:17,730 --> 00:16:22,230
You must have been frantic
with me pushing you so hard, right?

109
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:30,700
Still, I think it's admirable that you didn't run away
and saw it through to the end.

110
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:02,310
But Sunwoo,

111
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:06,730
what have you been staring at since earlier?

112
00:17:10,359 --> 00:17:13,950
If you stay completely frozen like that outside of work too,

113
00:17:16,369 --> 00:17:18,750
it's no fun for me.

114
00:17:46,650 --> 00:17:49,110
Ah... Ah.

115
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:51,990
M... Mr. Kang.
I'm... I'm, I'm sorry.

116
00:17:51,990 --> 00:17:54,780
Ah, what did I... just do...

117
00:17:54,780 --> 00:17:58,580
I'm sorry...
I must have lost my mind, seriously ah...

118
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,920
There's no need to apologize.

119
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:12,050
Because it wasn't bad.

120
00:18:17,810 --> 00:18:20,020
It's raining heavily,

121
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:24,100
so go to sleep now. Get a good rest,

122
00:18:24,980 --> 00:18:26,810
and I'll see you tomorrow.

123
00:18:51,050 --> 00:18:56,510
If you act like this, seriously,
how am I supposed to hold back...

124
00:19:04,730 --> 00:19:09,400
Yes, this is the design blueprint for our VVIP Ocean View Lounge,
focusing on efficiency and convenience.

125
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:13,030
Yes, that concludes my presentation. Thank you.

126
00:19:23,950 --> 00:19:25,370
Mr. Lee.

127
00:19:27,790 --> 00:19:31,090
- Are you kidding me?
- Pardon?

128
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:36,010
Ah... no. Um...
I completely revised it as you pointed out, Mr. Kang...

129
00:19:36,010 --> 00:19:38,390
And you call this a revision?

130
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:45,560
I told you to remove the point wall,
and you turned the space into a warehouse.

131
00:19:47,190 --> 00:19:54,110
I'm sure I told you clearly that
just because a design is pretty doesn't make it a good space.

132
00:19:54,820 --> 00:19:59,910
- You're lacking the basics, the basics!
- Mr. Kang, but I stayed up all night...

133
00:19:59,910 --> 00:20:01,530
Haa...

134
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:03,120
What?

135
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:07,120
Is your brain not working because you're tired from staying up all night?

136
00:20:10,330 --> 00:20:13,840
Standing in front of a client with this kind of result

137
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:19,260
is not just a matter of your own pride,
it's an insult to our entire team.

138
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:22,930
Do it again.

139
00:20:23,810 --> 00:20:30,150
If it's still at this level by tomorrow,
you are off this project, Mr. Lee.

140
00:20:35,610 --> 00:20:38,280
I will keep that in mind.

141
00:20:43,330 --> 00:20:46,540
Where are you going? The meeting isn't over yet.

142
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:49,290
I'm going to step out to the restroom for a moment.

143
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:53,340
I think I need to splash some cold water on my face
and get my head working.

144
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:55,840
I apologize.

145
00:20:58,130 --> 00:21:02,930
Mr. Kang... I've been working so much overtime lately,
I guess I'm out of my mind.

146
00:21:03,890 --> 00:21:06,310
You were never in your right mind.

147
00:21:07,770 --> 00:21:11,140
We'll resume in 10 minutes, so everyone take a break.

148
00:21:26,830 --> 00:21:32,000
Team Leader Kang Dojin...
Just how far will you push someone to the bottom...

149
00:21:46,850 --> 00:21:51,730
So, is your brain working now
that you've splashed some cold water on it?

150
00:21:52,270 --> 00:21:58,730
Mr. Kang, no matter how terrible my proposal was,
doing that in front of the entire team...

151
00:21:59,900 --> 00:22:02,950
Since I trampled on you like that,

152
00:22:02,950 --> 00:22:06,030
you're finally glaring at me like a wild beast.

153
00:22:08,410 --> 00:22:12,750
Rather than pretending to be a clumsily polite subordinate...

154
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:20,210
it's much better when you act so wronged
that you look ready to bite.

155
00:22:26,970 --> 00:22:28,970
Are you mad?

156
00:22:31,810 --> 00:22:34,810
You started this, Mr. Kang.

157
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:55,120
Mmm hmmm...
Mmhmm... Mmm...

158
00:23:36,250 --> 00:23:42,420
Twisted Tie
